#: site:site.about.lead
msgid "site.about.lead"
msgstr "Who sells Zabuno, what it is, how it is paid for and how to reach a person about it."

#: site:site.about.payment.body
msgid "site.about.payment.body"
msgstr "Paid plans are paid by card, through the payment service provider Iyzico. We do not accept bank transfer, cash or payment on delivery for a subscription, and we never see or store your card number: it is entered on the provider's own pages. Which card brands the provider accepts is set in the provider's own configuration, so it is not listed here."

#: site:site.about.payment.heading
msgid "site.about.payment.heading"
msgstr "Payment methods we accept"

#: site:site.about.reach.body
msgid "site.about.reach.body"
msgstr "Write to us with the contact form or to the e-mail address above. We keep every message and reply to the address you give us."

#: site:site.about.reach.cta
msgid "site.about.reach.cta"
msgstr "Open the contact form"

#: site:site.about.reach.heading
msgid "site.about.reach.heading"
msgstr "How to reach us"

#: site:site.about.seller.body
msgid "site.about.seller.body"
msgstr "These are the details of the legal entity that sells the paid plans and is the seller named in the Distance Sales Agreement."

#: site:site.about.seller.heading
msgid "site.about.seller.heading"
msgstr "The seller"

#: site:site.about.service.body
msgid "site.about.service.body"
msgstr "Zabuno is a subscription to a workspace in which a restaurant, cafe or bar keeps its menu and publishes it behind a permanent QR code. Changing a price or hiding a dish updates the page the guests see; the printed code stays the same."

#: site:site.about.service.heading
msgid "site.about.service.heading"
msgstr "What Zabuno is"

#: site:site.about.service.scope
msgid "site.about.service.scope"
msgstr "Depending on the plan, the workspace also covers branches, tables and QR codes, guest ordering, guest rating, team members with their own permissions, custom branding, reporting, and importing a menu from a photograph with a person confirming the result. The service is used through a web browser; nothing is installed."

